# A stall must answer HTTP 200, not 404. A 404 fallback is a shop that
# crawlers and link unfurlers read as gone, and the shared link is the whole
# product.
#
# The destination is "/" and not "/index.html". Pages answers a request for an
# .html URL with a 308 to its extensionless form, so a rewrite aimed at
# /index.html never resolves: the request falls through to 404.html instead,
# and every stall link returns 404. Measured against the Pages emulator and
# against a deployed origin, not inferred — the interaction is undocumented.
#
# Scoped to /s/* on purpose. A bare /* rewrite would serve the document for a
# missing hashed asset, which means HTML delivered as JavaScript.
/s/* / 200

# www belongs in a Cloudflare Redirect Rule, not here: a _redirects source must
# be a path beginning with "/", so a rule written against a hostname is ignored.
# One origin either way, or browser storage splits in two.
